---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms | Nether"
  description="Plain-language terms for using Nether and its articles, product information, and external links."
>
  <main class="archive-page plain-page">
    <header class="archive-header">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p>
        These terms explain the basic expectations for using Nether. By using
        the site, you agree to use it responsibly and in line with applicable
        law.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Using Nether</h2>
      <p>
        You may read and link to the site's pages for personal and informational
        use. Do not use the site to break the law, disrupt its operation, or
        try to gain access to systems or information that are not made
        available to you.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Content and other people's work</h2>
      <p>
        Articles, explanations, ratings, and other original material are
        published for readers of Nether. Please ask before republishing a
        substantial part of that work. Short quotations with a link back to the
        source are welcome where allowed by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Product names, logos, photographs, and other third-party materials
        belong to their respective owners. Their appearance on the site does
        not mean those owners sponsor or endorse Nether.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Information and opinions</h2>
      <p>
        I aim to make the information useful and clear, but specifications,
        prices, availability, and software can change. Ratings are opinions
        based on the criteria described in
        <a href="/gear/how-i-rate/">How I rate gear</a>. Some gear scores are
        based on specifications and reviewer consensus rather than hands-on
        use; the individual page should make that distinction clear.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on Nether is professional, financial, medical, or purchasing
        advice. Check important details with the manufacturer or seller and
        decide what fits your own needs.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>External links and purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to external pages, including Shopee, Lazada, and Amazon.
        I do not control those sites, their content, prices, availability,
        privacy practices, or terms. A purchase is made with the store, under
        its terms. Some product links may be affiliate links; read the
        <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> and
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> pages for more information.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        I work to keep Nether useful, but I cannot promise that every page will
        always be available, complete, or free of errors. To the extent
        applicable law allows, Nether is not responsible for losses caused by
        relying only on changing site information or by using a third-party
        site. Nothing in these terms limits a right or responsibility that
        cannot legally be limited.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        The site and these terms may change as the project develops. Updates
        will appear on this page with a revised date. For a question or
        correction, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> and
        <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> pages cover related practices.
      </p>
    </section>
    <p class="legal-updated">
      Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
